Description: Implements bivariate semi-parametric accelerated failure time
    models for the joint regression analysis of survival time and
    quality-adjusted survival time: the model proposed in da Silva (2026,
    doctoral thesis, University of Sao Paulo) and the model of Fine and
    Gelber (2001) <doi:10.1111/j.0006-341X.2001.00376.x>. Parameters are
    estimated via rank-based estimating equations, with
    inverse-probability-of-censoring weights for informative censoring and
    variance estimation by jackknife or bootstrap. Also provides the
    estimator of Zhao and Tsiatis (1997) <doi:10.1093/biomet/84.2.339> for
    the survival curve of the quality-adjusted time.
